Thought:[32;1m[1;3mFinal Answer:
Let $x_{ij}$ be a binary variable equal to 1 if machine $i$ is assigned to task $j$, and 0 otherwise.

Let $i \in \{\text{M1}, \text{M2}, \text{M3}, \text{M4}, \text{M5}, \text{M6}, \text{M7}, \text{M8}, \text{M9}, \text{M10}, \text{M11}, \text{M12}\}$ (machines) and $j \in \{\text{A}, \text{B}, \text{C}, \text{D}, \text{E}, \text{F}, \text{G}, \text{H}, \text{I}, \text{J}, \text{K}, \text{L}\}$ (tasks).

Let $c_{ij}$ be the cost of assigning machine $i$ to task $j$, as given below.

Minimize total assignment cost:
\[
\min \sum_{i \in \{\text{M1},\ldots,\text{M12}\}} \sum_{j \in \{\text{A},\ldots,\text{L}\}} c_{ij} x_{ij}
\]

Subject to:

Each machine is assigned to exactly one task:
\[
\sum_{j \in \{\text{A},\ldots,\text{L}\}} x_{ij} = 1 \quad \forall i \in \{\text{M1},\ldots,\text{M12}\}
\]

Each task is assigned to exactly one machine:
\[
\sum_{i \in \{\text{M1},\ldots,\text{M12}\}} x_{ij} = 1 \quad \forall j \in \{\text{A},\ldots,\text{L}\}
\]

Binary assignment variables:
\[
x_{ij} \in \{0,1\} \quad \forall i, j
\]

